<header><p class="st-kicker">county · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Viscounty of Carcassonne</h1><p class="st-meta">1067 CE – 1209 CE (approx.) · capital Carcassonne</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Trencavel viscounties of Carcassonne, Béziers and Albi, the heart of Cathar country, destroyed by the Albigensian Crusade in 1209.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1067 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raymond-bernard-trencavel">Raymond Bernard Trencavel</a>, viscount of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albi">Albi</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nimes">Nîmes</a>, gained <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carcassonne">Carcassonne</a> through his wife Ermengard, heiress of the counts of Carcassonne. Their son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bernard-ato-iv-trencavel">Bernard Ato IV</a> built a principality across Carcassonne, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beziers">Béziers</a>, Albi and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/razes">Razès</a>, balancing between the counts of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/county-of-toulouse">Toulouse</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-trencavel">Trencavels</a> ruled from the walled city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carcassonne">Carcassonne</a>, a centre of Occitan courtly culture. Their lands were the heartland of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catharism">Catharism</a>, and the viscounts tolerated the dissident church and its followers among the nobility. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romanesque-architecture">Romanesque</a> castle within Carcassonne's walls was their seat.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1209 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albigensian-crusade">Albigensian Crusade</a> sacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beziers">Béziers</a> and besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carcassonne">Carcassonne</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raymond-roger-trencavel">Raymond-Roger Trencavel</a> surrendered and died in prison, and his lands went to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-de-montfort-5th-earl-of-leicester">Simon de Montfort</a>. After a failed revolt in 1240 they were absorbed by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-france">Kingdom of France</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="county, 1067 CE – 1209 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">county</p><p class="st-emblem-region">France and the Low Countries</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:80.94%;width:2.83%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1067 CE – 1209 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>county</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Carcassonne</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Bernard Ato IV, Raymond-Roger Trencavel</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity and Catharism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Occitan</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Trencavel viscounties, Viscounty of Béziers and Carcassonne</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1138&amp;focus=viscounty-of-carcassonne" aria-label="Viscounty of Carcassonne on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4737 644 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Viscounty of Carcassonne lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5057 900L5035 888M5057 900L4984 945M5057 900L5054 728"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5035 888h0M4984 945h0M5054 728h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5057 900h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5057 900h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Carcassonne. <a href="/atlas?year=1138&amp;focus=viscounty-of-carcassonne">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

